Right that’s where I’m confused 

```

    params.MainnetGenesisHash: {
        BlockNumber: 15537393,
        BlockHash:   common.HexToHash("0x55b11b918355b1ef9c5db810302ebad0bf2544255b530cdce90674d5887bb286"),
    },
    // sepolia
    params.SepoliaGenesisHash: {
        BlockNumber: 1450409,
        BlockHash:   common.HexToHash("0x229f6b18ca1552f1d5146deceb5387333f40dc6275aebee3f2c5c4ece07d02db"),
    },
}
```

On Sepolia this prunes up to the transition block (first pos block) and prunes the terminal pow block.

Whereas on Mainnet that number prunes up to the terminal pow block and doesn’t prune the terminal pow block.

I’m not deep enough in the protocol to say whether that’s an issue. To prune less on mainnet seems fine; I don’t know whether era1 in Sepolia contains the terminal pow block - if it does it’s also fine.

There’s a part of me that really likes consistency across chains and clients - do or do not prune the terminal pow block. And, not a hill I’m defending particularly strongly.
